ull},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-29T09:00:04Z","updated_at":"2026-03-29T14:19:17Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.7.dev3.official [60fff00a6]\n\n### System information\n\nw11\n\n### Issue description\n\nI'm sorry, I don't know what to call this error.\nIt’s simply a bit painful to work with the tilemap layer node, I recently reported 2 bugs/problems, and now this one is added to them.\n\nProblem:\nIn the tilemap dock.\nYou center your tilemap to have a wide view.\nNow change to another of your tilemaps.\nNow the new tilemap appears off-center.\n\nSolution:\nGodot should remember in which centering position each tilemap is.\nIt should also remember it between sessions, meaning if I close Godot and open it later, all tilemaps are shown exactly as I left them.\n\nObserve this gif (press play), I have to be centering the two tilemaps because when centering one of them, it de-centers the other.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/70249da1-b091-46ec-8e42-02390f9e7e8f)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSee the gif\n\nOpen the TileMap editor dock for a specific TileMapLayer.\nPan or center the view to get a clear overview of your tiles.\nSwitch to a different TileMapLayer node in the Scene tree.\nThe view for the new TileMap appears offset/off-center because it inherits the position from the previous one.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n...","closed_by":null,"r